## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook **"coverage-touching"** test suite. Every production method is called (→ 95% coverage), but almost nothing is actually verified. These tests will pass even if the production code is completely broken.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Missing Assertions (tests prove nothing)

**1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)** — Fire-and-forget, zero assertions.
```csharp
// CURRENT: calls AddProduct, asserts nothing
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// FIX:
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(retrieved);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved.Price);
```

**2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 31)** — Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the price changed.
```csharp
// FIX: verify the side effect
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

**3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)** — Calls `RemoveProduct` but never checks the product is gone.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)** — Captures count into a local variable, never asserts on it. Also calls on an empty catalog, so even a broken impl returning 0 passes.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
var count = _catalog.GetProductCount();
Assert.AreEqual(1, count);
```

**5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)** — Applies a 10% discount, never checks any price changed.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
var p1 = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
var p2 = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002");
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, p1!.Price);   // 9.99 * 0.9
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, p2!.Price);  // 19.99 * 0.9
```

**6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 84)** — Imports a CSV line, never verifies the product was actually created.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var product = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(product);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", product.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, product.Price);
```

