**Root cause:** Every test follows the same template — call the method, optionally `Assert.IsNotNull` on the return value, done. This inflates line coverage to ~95% while verifying almost zero business logic. The suite would pass identically if `Save()` was a no-op, `UpdatePrice` didn't change the price, or `RemoveProduct` did nothing.
